  "pride_metadata": {
    "project": {
      "accession": "PXD071717",
      "title": "Quantitative Proteomic Profiling of Pinctada fucata Shell Nacre Defines a Solubility-based Type Classification of Shell Matrix Proteins",
      "additionalAttributes": [],
      "projectDescription": "This project investigates the shell matrix proteome of the nacreous layer of the pearl oyster Pinctada fucata. Nacre powders were subjected to an optimized extraction workflow combining EDTA-mediated decalcification and SDS/DTT-based solubilization to obtain three fractions: EDTA-soluble matrix (ESM), SDS-soluble matrix (SSM) and insoluble matrix (ISM). Each fraction was analysed by nanoLC-MS/MS using data-independent acquisition (DIA), and proteins were identified and quantified using a complete genome-derived database with intensity-based absolute quantification (iBAQ). The resulting dataset provides fraction-resolved protein abundances, solubility-based type classifications and functional annotations (including BLAST and conserved domain searches), and serves as a quantitative reference for comparative studies of molluscan shell biomineralization.",
      "sampleProcessingProtocol": "ESM and SSM were diluted to 100 \u00b5L with 7 M guanidine hydrochloride, 0.01 M EDTA, and 0.05 M Tris-HCl buffer (pH 8.0), and 1 \u00b5L of 0.5 M DTT was added. The reduction reaction was carried out at 60\u00b0C for 30 min. Afterward, 2 \u00b5L of 0.5 M iodoacetamide (FJIFILM Wako Pure Chemical) solution was added, and the mixture was stirred at room temperature in the dark for 1 h. Subsequently, 400 \u00b5L of methanol, 100 \u00b5L of chloroform (FJIFILM Wako Pure Chemical), and 300 \u00b5L of pure water were added in this order and vortex-mixed. After centrifugation (14,000 rpm, 5 min, 4\u00b0C), the supernatant was discarded. On ice, 300 \u00b5L of methanol was added to the lower phase and mixed by inversion, followed by centrifugation (15,000 rpm, 3 min, 4\u00b0C). The supernatant was removed, and the protein pellet was then resuspended with 200 \u00b5L of 70% ethanol (FJIFILM Wako Pure Chemical) and further centrifuged (12,000 rpm, 3 min, 4\u00b0C). The supernatant was discarded, and the pellet was completely dried using a rotary evaporator. The sample was dissolved by adding 13 \u00b5L of pure water, followed by the addition of 26 \u00b5L of 50 mM NH\u2084HCO\u2083 (Nacalai Tesque, Kyoto, Japan) (pH 8.0) and 5 \u00b5L of 100 ng/\u00b5L Trypsin Platinum solution (Promega, Madison, WI, USA). The protein was digested at 37\u00b0C for 24 hours, and 1 \u00b5L of 4% trifluoroacetic acid (TFA) (FJIFILM Wako Pure Chemical) was added. The digestion solution was concentrated via rotary evaporation and prepared as an LC-MS/MS sample. The ISM was boiled in 10 mL of 10 mM DTT (FJIFILM Wako Pure Chemical) for 10 min, and the 20 mM iodoacetamide (FJIFILM Wako Pure Chemical) was added. The mixture was stirred at room temperature in the dark for 1 h. After centrifugation to remove unreacted iodoacetamide, the precipitate was suspended in 1 mL of 50 mM NH\u2084HCO\u2083 (Nacalai Tesque) solution. Additionally, 6 \u00b5L of 1 \u00b5g/\u00b5L Trypsin Platinum (Promega) solution was added, and the mixture was stirred at 37\u00b0C for 48 hours to digest the proteins. The supernatant was applied to a Sep-Pak C18 column (Merck) to purify peptides. The purified peptides were dried and dissolved in 0.1% TFA (FJIFILM Wako Pure Chemical).",
      "dataProcessingProtocol": "Raw LC\u2013MS/MS data were processed using MaxQuant with the built-in Andromeda search engine. Peak lists were searched against a Pinctada fucata protein database derived from the complete genome assembly, assuming trypsin specificity and allowing missed cleavages. Carbamidomethylation of cysteine was set as a fixed modification, and oxidation of methionine and protein N-terminal acetylation were set as variable modifications. Peptide- and protein-level false discovery rates were controlled at 1% using a target\u2013decoy strategy, and common contaminants, reverse hits and proteins identified only by site were removed prior to quantification. Protein abundances were calculated as intensity-based absolute quantification (iBAQ) values, and downstream filtering, normalization and calculation of derived quantitative indices were performed in Perseus (version 2.0.7.0).",
